1
00:00:00,174 --> 00:00:02,084
What if chai vanished
from India overnight?

2
00:00:02,204 --> 00:00:04,154
India drinks most of the tea it grows.

3
00:00:04,355 --> 00:00:07,145
Every morning,
hundreds of millions of cups are poured.

4
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:08,200
Start with the stalls.

5
00:00:08,386 --> 00:00:11,036
Countless roadside chai
sellers outside offices,

6
00:00:11,286 --> 00:00:14,796
bus stands and railway stations
would lose their only income.

7
00:00:14,821 --> 00:00:15,711
Then the farms.

8
00:00:15,862 --> 00:00:18,612
Assam, Darjeeling and
the Nilgiris grow tea,

9
00:00:18,902 --> 00:00:21,172
and more than a million
workers depend on the estates.

10
00:00:21,517 --> 00:00:22,427
Then the mornings.

11
00:00:22,582 --> 00:00:24,452
Chai is how Indians welcome guests,

12
00:00:24,842 --> 00:00:26,152
close deals and sit with friends.

13
00:00:26,293 --> 00:00:28,083
Without it, the tapri conversation,

14
00:00:28,313 --> 00:00:31,118
the office break and the long
train wait would go quiet.

15
00:00:31,118 --> 00:00:34,408
And a century ago,
most Indians didn't drink tea every day.

16
00:00:34,429 --> 00:00:36,879
It became India's drink
in just a few generations.

17
00:00:37,234 --> 00:00:39,364
It's only a cup of tea, until it's gone.

18
00:00:39,434 --> 00:00:41,184
So what if chai vanished from India?

